<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kedatuan of Dapitan</h1><p class="st-meta">1300 CE – 1563 CE (approx.) · capital Dapitan (Bohol)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Visayan polity on Bohol whose people, after a raid from Ternate around 1563, moved to northern Mindanao and gave their name to Dapitan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dapitan is known from Spanish accounts, especially the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-combes">Francisco Combes</a>, and from Boholano tradition. It was a settlement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohol">Bohol</a> coast, probably on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panglao-island">Panglao Island</a>, ruled by datus and trading with other Visayan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a> ports. Its founding date is unknown.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Spanish sources describe a prosperous community of seafarers, traders and boat builders, led by datus over freemen and dependants, with indigenous religion and ties to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rajahnate-of-butuan">Butuan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cebu">Cebu</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1563 raiders from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ternate-sultanate">Ternate</a>, perhaps with Portuguese help, attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohol">Bohol</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/datu-pagbuaya">Datu Pagbuaya</a> led many of the survivors to the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a>, where they founded Dapitan, in today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamboanga-del-norte">Zamboanga del Norte</a>. Pagbuaya later helped the Spanish, and Dapitan became an early mission centre.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kedatuan-of-dapitan.jpg" alt="Kedatuan of Dapitan" width="320" height="444"><figcaption>Image: Boxer Codex · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naturales_4.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1300 CE – 1563 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dapitan (Bohol)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pagbuaya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Indigenous Philippine religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Boholano Cebuano</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/philippines">Philippines</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dapitan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1432&amp;focus=kedatuan-of-dapitan" aria-label="Kedatuan of Dapitan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8090 1854 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kedatuan of Dapitan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8410 2110L8538 2404"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8538 2404h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8410 2110h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8410 2110h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dapitan. <a href="/atlas?year=1432&amp;focus=kedatuan-of-dapitan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

